    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "94a55e7e-bdd7-593b-b741-56f917ef431e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y+z &=0 \\\\ 4x-7y+2z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cb083785-606d-598b-be9c-84053f8ce228",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6f81e569-22a6-5fa2-96b1-ca91eabab34b",
