  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "44b79283-8e9d-5db1-acb1-49a8325c302c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x-2y &=7 \\\\ 2x+3y &=11 \\\\ 5x+y &=40\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system has a unique solution",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 11 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 40\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 11 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 25 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 40\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 75\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "38444906-c7a4-5a04-b411-332fbecec1aa",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
